WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.570
Welcome back to Learn Text.js.

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.380
This is chapter nine:
Running in a Terminal.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.890
The same app runs in a real terminal.

4
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.700
Layout, components, keymaps
and route handlers are shared,

5
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.290
and they render into
the same grid of cells.

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.290
Only the last step changes.

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.970
In the console, cells become
%c-styled spans in a console.log call.

8
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.500
In a terminal, they become
truecolor ANSI escape codes.

9
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.700
Let's run it in a terminal.

10
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.730
Add a script to package.json
that runs text run.

11
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.660
This one is called tui.

12
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.290
bun run tui draws the app full-screen,
starting at the root route.

13
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.850
text run imports every file in app,

14
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.970
and mounts the App Router
with an in-memory history.

15
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.530
Link, useRouter, notFound
and redirect work unchanged.

16
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.890
Press 2, and the link
goes to /deployments.

17
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.690
Same-origin fetch calls to /api
run your route handlers in-process,

18
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.530
so the table has its data.

19
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.570
Ctrl+C quits and restores your scrollback.

20
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.020
text run needs Bun.

21
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.820
Next, quit with Q.

22
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.330
Terminal users expect Q to quit.

23
00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.410
Import useApp from @textjs/app.

24
00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:33.610
Call it in the root layout, and when
the input is Q, call app.exit().

25
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.490
exit unmounts the app and
restores the terminal.

26
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.980
In the browser, it
unmounts the console app.

27
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.730
On the lesson page, the
console plays the terminal.

28
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.690
Click the pad first,
so the page has focus.

29
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.010
Press Enter to start text run.

30
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.780
The arrow keys move the selection,
and Q quits back to the shell.

31
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.500
You can also write your own CLI.

32
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.170
For a single component,
use renderToTerminal.

33
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:10.850
Import it from @textjs/app/terminal,
along with the component.

34
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.650
Pass it an element, and
it draws full-screen.

35
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:20.260
waitUntilExit resolves when the app
exits, for example after useApp().exit().

36
00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.900
Finally, what's different in a terminal.

37
00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.250
To start on another route, pass --path.

38
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:36.170
In a terminal, frames repaint at up to 60
a second, where the console gets about 15.

39
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.850
The grid is sized to the window,
instead of the docked console.

40
00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.050
Images need pixel data instead of a URL.

41
00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.420
Everything else, including this
dashboard, is the same code.

42
00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.690
Quick check.

43
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:54.100
What changes when the
app runs in a terminal?

44
00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.690
Only the output: ANSI instead of %c spans.

45
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.650
Layout, components, keymaps
and route handlers are shared.

46
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.460
Only the final encoding differs.

47
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.940
And how does an app quit itself?

48
00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.510
useApp().exit().

49
00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.480
exit unmounts the app and
restores the terminal.

50
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.030
Next, in chapter ten, the last one,

51
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.110
you'll build Acme Deploys,
set its metadata and ship it.

52
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.760
See you there.
